[![make.fun · gta6-01](https://make.fun/badge/gta6-01.svg)](https://make.fun/bounty/gta6-01?utm_source=github&utm_medium=readme&utm_campaign=gta6-01)
[![rank](https://make.fun/badge/gta6-01/waz5211/gta6-01/rank.svg)](https://make.fun/bounty/gta6-01/leaderboard?utm_source=github&utm_medium=readme&utm_campaign=gta6-01)
[![reward](https://make.fun/badge/gta6-01/waz5211/gta6-01/reward.svg)](https://make.fun/bounty/gta6-01?utm_source=github&utm_medium=readme&utm_campaign=gta6-01)

**Port Meridian** — a sun-soaked open-world crime game in the browser. You are Rook, a driver for hire in the fictional coastal city of Port Meridian, taking jobs from fixer Marla Voss. Explore the city on foot or by car, steal parked cars and traffic, outrun the Port Meridian PD under a five-star wanted system, fight the Harlow crew with fists and a pistol, and run three linked story missions — a first fare, a 90-second deadline delivery, and a heat-wave getaway — then keep earning with side jobs. Traffic and pedestrians live their own lives, the HUD carries a live minimap, and every sound is synthesized with WebAudio. Everything is 100% original: its own city, characters, vehicles, names and story.

## Run it

```sh
node serve.ts
```

Then open http://localhost:8080 in desktop Chrome. No build step, no network — the game is static files under `game/`.

